Tag the opener service so core's OpenerResolver can find it.

Since Drupal 10.3 the media library resolves openers through a service
collector (tag media_library.opener) instead of looking them up by id in the
container, so an untagged opener throws "must be an instance of
MediaLibraryOpenerInterface" when the dialog opens.

diff --git a/linkit_media_library.services.yml b/linkit_media_library.services.yml
--- a/linkit_media_library.services.yml
+++ b/linkit_media_library.services.yml
@@ -2,3 +2,5 @@ services:
   linkit_media_library.opener.editor:
     class: Drupal\linkit_media_library\LinkitMediaLibraryEditorOpener
     arguments: ['@entity_type.manager']
+    tags:
+      - { name: media_library.opener }
